+# Past decisions: selective evidence leads
+
+Optional lookup for SkillForge's own history, checked 2026-11-07. Use the [attempt index](Index.md) for other records. This map is not an exhaustive review or new mandatory retrieval step. Open supporting records before making a consequential claim. Project paths below are optional external evidence; if unavailable, report that limit rather than inventing observations.
+
+| Decision now | Relevant observation / condition | Evidence and implication |
+|---|---|---|
+| Make preselected lessons a standard improvement step? | In the real Fabric comparison both selectors chose the same L1/L2 packet; ordinary authors independently read those lessons. All six repairs passed primary checks; adjacent coverage varied. | Project `20-working-T1-T3/LessonRetrieval20261106/report.md`. Mandatory retrieval and selector superiority were not supported. This small four-card history does not settle retrieval from a scattered archive. Count packet preparation and ordinary access in a new comparison. |
+| Repeat selector trials to confirm the broader repair? | Delivered content was identical, so different artifact coverage cannot identify a content-selection effect. The later continuation task's three methods all stopped/reframed. | Project `20-working-T1-T3/Discriminating20261106/report.md`. Do not repeat the unchanged selector contrast. Ordinary-history versus common-packet cost/use remains a separate question; missing author/exposure provenance stays missing. |
+| Replace the full method with the short practical control? | All three methods passed 58/58 repair and 6/6 consumer checks. Short control was descriptively fastest in single concurrent observations. | Same Discriminating report. Preserve it as a credible comparator, not a proven replacement or causal cost ranking. |
+| Claim idea generation improves solutions or loading? | Both methods found useful caches and splits. Original focused context did not load GenerateAlternatives; repaired activation later worked, but outcomes still tied and returned loading was mixed/worse. | [Generation record](IdeaGeneration/Record.md), [activation record](FocusedActivation/Record.md); project `20-working-T1-T3/RealSkillComparison20261106/Results.md` and `Activation20261106/Results.md`. Keep activation, output benefit and author effort separate. No general superiority. |
+| Infer efficiency from a shorter workflow or compact records? | Operational Update text shrank, but full-task input/output costs increased; useful outputs tied. Ordinary candidate execution did not use the optional compact template; a separate recovery test did. | [Operational record](OperationalEfficiency/Record.md); project `20-working-T1-T3/OperationalEfficiency20261106/FinalResults.md`. Measure actual task effort and distinguish adoption from usability; do not use word count as runtime savings. |
+| Treat an old uninstalled/no-merge statement as current? | November 7 integration supersedes deployment status, not trial observations or limits. Operational efficiency, alternative generation and experiment preflight are already present. | [Validation integration](../Evidence/ValidationSummary.md), [current index](Index.md). The runtime owner map was also integrated Nov 7. Verify current version before an operational action; historical cautions are not a present prohibition or new benefit evidence. |
+| Reuse v0.5/v0.6 guidance as a newly proven improvement? | Early discovery/proposal and planning tests saturated explicit synthetic contracts. Much of their reasoning is now present in later procedures. | Earlier entries in [Index](Index.md). Compare a distinct still-missing mechanism against current instructions; do not copy an obsolete package over newer protections. |
+| Regard a failed runner/audit as a failed candidate? | The preflight audit initially required PlanChange even for a valid EvaluateSkill path. Operational trials also preserved setup/path errors before completed outcomes. | Discriminating and OperationalEfficiency reports above. Keep process failures and established outcome evidence separate; a later repair does not fabricate missing observations. |
+
+Separate observations, interpretation, applicability and the present decision in the existing task record. An unchanged conclusion is valid; the purpose is useful evidence use, not collecting more history. Scope of this map: selected SkillForge decisions from Nov 3–7. Later records may supersede particular claims; preserve the original observations and record exactly what changed.
